data.content:
Done. The component:

- **Is generic** (`@typeparam TItem`) — works with any item type.
- **Uses code-behind** — `.razor` for markup, `.razor.cs` for logic.
- **Doesn't mutate the input** — copies `Items` into an internal `_items` list on each parameter set.
- **Provides Move Up/Down buttons** — disabled at boundaries.
- **Notifies the parent** — fires `OnOrderChanged` with the reordered list as `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`.

Usage matches your example:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> newOrder)
    {
        tasks = newOrder.ToList();
    }
}
```
